From: R. Matthew Emerson <rme@acm.org>
Subject: [PATCH] TEST ONLY: sled the pre-fix unbind_interrupt_level window (32-bit ARM)

Test instrumentation for the unbind_interrupt_level missed-suspend
reproducer, PRE-FIX form, 32-bit ARM.  Holds open the window between
the pending-suspend flags test and the *INTERRUPT-LEVEL* restore, where
a suspend signal is deferred against the old level after the flags were
already read, so the unbind returns without delivering it.

Contributed by the maintainer on the pull request that adds this
directory, with the measurement: under this sled the kernel wedges.  A
worker takes SIGSEGV inside unbind_interrupt_level and then deadlocks on
the exception lock while the suspending thread waits for it to
acknowledge the suspend signal.  The 32-bit ARM failure is therefore not
only a latency spike: the pre-fix code also read a register it had never
loaded.

Applies to the tree BEFORE the 32-bit ARM fix.  Mutually exclusive with
the post-fix sled, which targets the restored instruction order.  NEVER
MERGE.
---

diff --git a/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s b/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s
index 174882e..4a43373 100644
--- a/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s
+++ b/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s
@@ -2683,6 +2683,12 @@ _spentry(unbind_interrupt_level)
 0:      
         __(ldr temp1,[imm0,#binding.val])
         __(ldr imm0,[imm0,#binding.link])
+        /* TEST ONLY, NEVER MERGE: hold the pre-fix window (flags read
+           -> *INTERRUPT-LEVEL* restore) open so a suspend can land in
+           it.  imm1 is dead here.  */
+        __(mov imm1,#0x400000)
+9:      __(subs imm1,imm1,#1)
+        __(bne 9b)
         __(str temp1,[temp2,#INTERRUPT_LEVEL_BINDING_INDEX])
         __(str imm0,[rcontext,#tcr.db_link])
         __(cmp temp0,#0)
